+# UC11 get permitted profile
+
+Issue12 / FR-PR-03, BR03/04/28. GET /api/profiles/{id} returns the active encrypted profile by canonical lowercase nonzero D-format public ID, with only visible recordIds/folderIds/collectionIds. Validate current owner identity, active account, terminal erasure and current account-wide or selected-profile session. A valid selected session can read only its selected profile. Hidden/foreign/trashed/erased/missing target404; invalid current session403; missing identity/access401; malformed path/header/query/body400; dependency or corrupt permitted stored metadata503. No reads mutate or disclose partial data; no-store.
+
+BR03/28 and the permission matrix mean collection grants expose included content through a recipient's OWN profile, never a foreign profile's unrelated encrypted metadata. No records/folders/collections/association/grant entities exist yet: persisted profiles necessarily have no links (UC09 rejects unresolved nonempty association arrays). Return truthful empty relationship arrays now; when those entities arrive, extend this same-snapshot projection with active/visible relationships before those flows release. Do not invent shared grants or synthesize foreign profiles.
+
+Read in one PostgreSQL statement with ownership, current session, selected scope, trash and terminal erasure predicates before projecting ciphertext. Validate target identity, positive safe revision/sequence, UTC microsecond time, strict encrypted envelope/wrapper shapes, profile grant ID/current content epoch and recipient authenticated identity. Reuse a shared query projection validator for UC10 and UC11 so the UC10 review recipient invariant cannot diverge. Preserve existing list ordering-corruption guard. Client decryptability and independent approvals remain deferred development-only; no new cryptographic audit claim.
+
+Route accepts raw string to return400 for malformed GUID instead of routing404. Reject all query keys, duplicate/empty malformed access header and any GET body including HTTP2 unknown length. Response data fields: profileId, revision, serverSequence, editedAt, envelope, keyWrappers, recordIds, folderIds, collectionIds. AF01 strict syntax; AF02 filtered404; AF03 current identity/session; AF04 real provider/table outage and corrupt stored results. Full unfiltered suite >=90% line coverage, branches reported; ordinary review and requiredCI gate authorized develop merge.
